 "text": "Hi, how you doing these days? I understand the feeling. Breaks keep us fresh, and at home you don't have the commute to counterbalance them. Set a schedule, like every hour or after each five minutes, and stick to it. A short walk, few presses of the keyboard, drink if you thirsty, your eyes from the screen, and then come right back. A few minutes off can prevent a long break turning into a drone. Leave it room somewhere out of sight. A handful of squats, a short yawn, or putting the dishes away counts too. Keep a record, and soon you'll find a rhythm that works.",
